## Young adults should expect to see growth in three primary areas:
{% /gridSquare %}

{% gridSquare
   contentType="color"
   backgroundColor="#3d2e1f"
   textColor="light"
   aspectRatio="square"
   width="auto"
   height="auto" %}
## Spiritually

Participants will be challenged to grow in their relationship with Christ and develop a desire to **become more like** **Jesus**—learning to follow Him in their work, relationships, decisions, and everyday lives
{% /gridSquare %}

{% gridSquare
   contentType="color"
   backgroundColor="#ffffff"
   textColor="dark"
   aspectRatio="square"
   width="auto"
   height="auto" %}
## Career Skill Development

Participants will explore their gifts, interests, and potential career paths while gaining practical experience. Through guided mentorship, Christian community, and job placement, they will develop the confidence needed to navigate future opportunities and responsibilities
{% /gridSquare %}

{% gridSquare
   contentType="color"
   backgroundColor="#3d2e1f"
   textColor="light"
   aspectRatio="square"
   width="auto"
   height="auto" %}
## Personally

Participants will be challenged through community living and real-life responsibilities to become more adaptable and develop problem solving skills. They will learn to take ownership, navigate challenges, communicate well, receive feedback, resolve conflict, and lead through service
{% /gridSquare %}
{% /squareGrid %}

{% section
   backgroundColor="cream"
   centered=true
   width="auto"
   height="auto" %}
# Summer Staff Skill Development Opportunities

**Bold participants will learn and develop a skill to use for Summer Camp programming:**

{% cardGrid cols="3" width="auto" height="auto" backgroundColor="#f5f0e8" %}
{% contentCard
   icon="Lightbulb"
   iconSize="lg"
   title="Recreation"
   headingLevel="3"
   width="auto"
   height="auto"
   backgroundColor="#f5f0e8" %}
Learn to lead games, activities, and recreational experiences that are designed to build relationships with campers and foster community
{% /contentCard %}

{% contentCard
   icon="Users"
   iconSize="lg"
   title="Waterfront"
   headingLevel="3"
   width="auto"
   height="auto"
   backgroundColor="#f5f0e8" %}
Train and develop the skills needed to safely supervise and lead campers in waterfront activities
{% /contentCard %}

{% contentCard
   icon="Mountain"
   iconSize="lg"
   title="Ropes Course "
   headingLevel="3"
   width="auto"
   height="auto"
   backgroundColor="#f5f0e8" %}
Learn to facilitate high-ropes and low-ropes activities with an emphasis on safety, teamwork, and confidence
{% /contentCard %}
{% /cardGrid %}
{% /section %}

{% section
   backgroundColor="cream"
   centered=true
   width="auto"
   height="auto" %}
{% cardGrid cols="3" width="auto" height="auto" backgroundColor="#f5f0e8" %}
{% contentCard
   icon="Shield"
   iconSize="lg"
   title="LIT Counselor "
   headingLevel="3"
   width="auto"
   height="auto"
   backgroundColor="#f5f0e8" %}
The LIT Counselor will learn to lead high school students in our Leaders in Training program to help them develop leadership skills, responsibility, and a heart for serving others
{% /contentCard %}

{% contentCard
   icon="CheckCircle"
   iconSize="lg"
   title="Food Service"
   headingLevel="3"
   width="auto"
   height="auto"
   backgroundColor="#f5f0e8" %}
Gain experience serving in the kitchen while learning the importance of teamwork, hospitality, cleanliness, and creating a welcoming environment for campers and staff
{% /contentCard %}

{% contentCard
   icon="Cross"
   iconSize="lg"
   title="Music and Worship"
   headingLevel="3"
   width="auto"
   height="auto"
   backgroundColor="#f5f0e8" %}
Develop skills in leading worship through music, preparing worship experiences, and helping campers engage with God through biblical and Christ-centered worship
{% /contentCard %}
{% /cardGrid %}
{% /section %}

{% section
   backgroundColor="cream"
   centered=true
   width="auto"
   height="auto" %}
{% cardGrid cols="3" width="auto" height="auto" backgroundColor="" %}
{% contentCard
   icon="ClipboardList"
   iconSize="lg"
   title="Administrative, Office, and Marketing"
   headingLevel="3"
   width="auto"
   height="auto"
   backgroundColor="#f5f0e8" %}
Learn the organizational and administrative skills that support camp operations, including communication, scheduling, registration, organization, and serving campers and families
{% /contentCard %}

{% contentCard
   icon="Leaf"
   iconSize="lg"
   title="Maintenance and Grounds"
   headingLevel="3"
   width="auto"
   height="auto"
   backgroundColor="#f5f0e8" %}
Gain hands-on experience caring for camp facilities and property through maintenance, grounds keeping, and improvement projects that help create a safe and welcoming camp environment
{% /contentCard %}

{% contentCard
   icon="Camera"
   iconSize="lg"
   title="Photo, Video, and Media"
   headingLevel="3"
   width="auto"
   height="auto"
   backgroundColor="#f5f0e8" %}
Learn to capture and create photos, videos, and other media that tell the story of camp, highlight what God is doing, and communicate the camp experience to families and the broader community
{% /contentCard %}
